{"slug":"longest-arithmetic-subsequence","title":"The Longest Subsequence With a Constant Step","topic":"dp","difficulty":"medium","order":746,"tags":["dp","subsequence","arithmetic-progression","two-dimensional"],"timeLimitMs":2000,"concept":{"title":"The state is (last position, common difference)","body":["Choose some numbers from a list, keeping their order, so that the chosen numbers form an **arithmetic progression** (the difference between neighbours is the same everywhere). What is the largest number of chosen numbers? For `3 6 9 12` it is 4. For `9 4 7 2 10` it is 3 (`4 7 10` with the step 3). Unlike in the stretches problem, the numbers need **not** be next to each other.","The last chosen number alone does not tell what the next one can be, but the last number together with the **common difference** does. Let `best(j, d)` be the length of the longest arithmetic subsequence that ends at the position `j` and has the step `d`. A subsequence ending at `j` with the step `d` came from some earlier position `i` with `a[i] = a[j] - d`: if there is a subsequence ending at `i` with the same step, we extend it, **`best(j, d) = best(i, d) + 1`**; otherwise `(i, j)` is a new pair of length 2. The difference is between -500 and 500, so there are at most 1001 steps.",{"code":"best = [[0] * 1001 for _ in range(n)]        # best[j][d + 500]: 0 means \"no pair with this step yet\"\nanswer = 1\nfor j in range(n):\n    for i in range(j):\n        d = a[j] - a[i] + 500\n        best[j][d] = max(best[j][d], best[i][d] + 1 if best[i][d] else 2)\n        answer = max(answer, best[j][d])\nprint(answer)"},"Every pair `(i, j)` is looked at once, so the time is O(n^2), about half a million steps, and the memory O(n * 1001). A single number is an arithmetic progression of length 1, so the answer is at least 1. When values are small, an array indexed by the difference is simpler and faster than a hash table."]},"statement":["A list of `n` integers is given. Print the length of the longest subsequence (numbers keep their order, but need not be neighbours) in which the difference between every two neighbouring chosen numbers is the same."],"inputFormat":["The first line has `n`: the number of values.","The second line has `n` numbers."],"outputFormat":["Print the length of the longest arithmetic subsequence."],"constraints":["1 <= n <= 1000","0 <= each number <= 500"],"examples":[{"input":"4\n3 6 9 12\n","output":"4\n","note":"All four numbers have the step 3: 4."},{"input":"5\n9 4 7 2 10\n","output":"3\n","note":"The numbers 4, 7, 10 have the step 3: 3."}],"hints":["A subsequence is described by its last position and its common difference.","For a pair (i, j), i < j, the difference is a[j] - a[i]; extend the best subsequence that ends at i with the same difference, if any.","Index the differences with an offset of 500 in an array."],"starter":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\n# Your code here\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    // Your code here\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = Long.parseLong(next());\n\n        // Your code here\n    }\n}\n"},"solution":{"explanation":["best(j, d) is the length of the longest arithmetic subsequence ending at the position j with the step d; for each pair i < j with d = a[j] - a[i] it is best(i, d) + 1 if that exists and 2 otherwise. The answer is the largest value (at least 1)."],"complexity":"Time O(n^2), space O(n * range of values).","code":{"python":"import sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\nn = int(input())\na = list(map(int, input().split()))\n\nbest = [[0] * 1001 for _ in range(n)]\nanswer = 1\nfor j in range(n):\n    row = best[j]\n    aj = a[j]\n    for i in range(j):\n        d = aj - a[i] + 500\n        length = best[i][d] + 1 if best[i][d] else 2\n        if length > row[d]:\n            row[d] = length\n            if length > answer:\n                answer = length\nprint(answer)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    long long n;\n    cin >> n;\n    vector<long long> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) cin >> a[i];\n\n    vector<vector<int>> best(n, vector<int>(1001, 0));\n    int answer = 1;\n    for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < j; i++) {\n            int d = (int)(a[j] - a[i] + 500);\n            int length = best[i][d] ? best[i][d] + 1 : 2;\n            if (length > best[j][d]) {\n                best[j][d] = length;\n                if (length > answer) answer = length;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    cout << answer << \"\\n\";\n\n    return 0;\n}\n","java":"import java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n    static StringTokenizer tokens = new StringTokenizer(\"\");\n\n    static String next() throws IOException {\n        while (!tokens.hasMoreTokens()) {\n            tokens = new StringTokenizer(in.readLine());\n        }\n        return tokens.nextToken();\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        long n = Long.parseLong(next());\n        long[] a = new long[(int) n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) a[i] = Long.parseLong(next());\n\n        int[][] best = new int[(int) n][1001];\n        int answer = 1;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {\n            for (int i = 0; i < j; i++) {\n                int d = (int) (a[j] - a[i] + 500);\n                int length = best[i][d] > 0 ? best[i][d] + 1 : 2;\n                if (length > best[j][d]) {\n                    best[j][d] = length;\n                    if (length > answer) answer = length;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(answer);\n    }\n}\n"}},"tests":[{"input":"4\n3 6 9 12\n","output":"4\n"},{"input":"5\n9 4 7 2 10\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"1\n5\n","output":"1\n"},{"input":"2\n1 500\n","output":"2\n"},{"input":"3\n7 7 7\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"10\n9 5 4 6 5 19 12 7 6 2\n","output":"3\n"},{"input":"100\n29 32 48 22 49 29 15 35 36 29 30 32 4 9 45 30 47 9 16 26 47 37 8 37 49 45 37 37 8 31 48 37 39 47 37 45 27 32 30 2 38 6 5 42 41 30 47 11 13 37 26 28 16 2 45 12 20 41 50 0 23 19 4 32 36 36 33 5 1 49 32 10 0 48 12 44 16 33 29 35 25 49 17 5 14 26 22 42 41 50 2 7 29 13 29 17 31 35 17 11\n","output":"7\n"},{"input":"300\n260 264 478 387 24 181 249 492 283 130 244 71 309 244 5 291 130 91 118 106 393 248 359 393 75 157 52 455 127 209 278 320 138 357 176 33 498 347 357 348 43 258 397 365 449 438 346 365 20 21 265 429 478 53 220 440 85 245 138 252 356 381 91 366 177 49 434 109 238 65 267 457 65 262 302 292 307 286 301 320 245 193 322 112 253 217 87 62 443 150 138 454 291 130 214 166 402 324 331 42 27 100 463 242 331 254 102 99 346 96 68 365 360 71 162 364 32 46 404 282 35 182 45 101 55 310 396 193 465 498 175 433 269 159 475 190 52 209 458 24 375 25 338 24 20 36 277 99 234 276 142 394 336 364 254 212 242 122 186 230 32 179 338 224 268 39 329 379 349 305 35 182 425 425 173 259 368 263 117 460